","datePublished":"Oct 2, 2026, 12:00:18 PM","dateUpdated":"Oct 2, 2026, 1:50:12 PM","baseScore":10.0,"baseScoreVersion":"4.0","baseScoreVector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:H/SI:H/SA:H/E:P","references":"https://vuldb.com/vuln/412917\nhttps://vuldb.com/vuln/412917/cti\nhttps://vuldb.com/cve/CVE-2026-104610\nhttps://vuldb.com/submit/962541\nhttps://github.com/Expl0rer-Ct/CVE/issues/1\nhttps://www.tenda.com.cn/\n","aliases":"GHSA-rw2m-x35c-9468\nCVE-2026-104610\n","assigner":"VulDB","epss":0.64,"enisaIdProduct":[{"id":"1ddeaa91-cc27-3f06-a32d-5a44d11f7287","product":{"name":"HG9","vendor":{"name":"Tenda"}},"product_version":"300001138_en_xpon"},{"id":"9cf7c59f-65c1-3f92-9cad-cf623d970edb","product":{"name":"HG7","vendor":{"name":"Tenda"}},"product_version":"300001138_en_xpon"},{"id":"d5e53c33-1759-3eaa-883a-f4124cece5d0","product":{"name":"HG10","vendor":{"name":"Tenda"}},"product_version":"300001138_en_xpon"}],"enisaIdVendor":[{"id":"c5d7b7b4-8ee4-3de2-aef8-198cff5b6448","vendor":{"name":"Tenda"}}]},{"id":"EUVD-2026-91574","enisaUuid":"a16e6460-ce0e-361c-9115-25c26a9abd14","description":"Uncaught exception, Improper Handling of Exceptional Conditions vulnerability in Apache Thrift Ruby bindings.\n\n\n\nThis issue affects Apache Thrift: before 0.25.0.\n\n\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 0.25.0, which fixes the issue.","datePublished":"Oct 2, 2026, 12:03:23 PM","dateUpdated":"Oct 2, 2026, 1:44:32 PM","baseScore":8.7,"baseScoreVersion":"4.0","baseScoreVector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N","references":"https://lists.apache.org/thread/33otcgbqd27wf6qq810q56znzbomnhg1\nhttps://lists.apache.org/thread/k1t5r9sz7k5tn57cnf5khw2ywlxv6098\n","aliases":"GHSA-vgfv-p7x2-fp2x\nCVE-2026-96277\n","assigner":"apache","epss":0.43,"enisaIdProduct":[{"id":"aba3ac80-aadf-3cd9-bc20-2a4dabfd511c","product":{"name":"Apache Thrift","vendor":{"name":"Apache Software Foundation"}},"product_version":"0 \u003c0.25.0"}],"enisaIdVendor":[{"id":"a4a317c2-0faa-33a7-a962-e0b08106f161","vendor":{"name":"Apache Software Foundation"}}]},{"id":"EUVD-2026-91482","enisaUuid":"79b3d935-60e2-308f-aabc-df5385938a70","description":"YesWiki before 4.6.7 contains an unrestricted file upload vulnerability that allows authenticated admins to write remote files into the web-accessible files/ directory via Bazar CSV import preview. Attackers can import a CSV whose file or image field references a remote .php URL, which is saved without extension checks and executed as server-side code.","datePublished":"Oct 2, 2026, 11:38:36 AM","dateUpdated":"Oct 2, 2026, 1:43:17 PM","baseScore":8.6,"baseScoreVersion":"4.0","baseScoreVector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:H/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N","references":"https://github.com/YesWiki/yeswiki/security/advisories/GHSA-v3gq-c7c6-mxw3\nhttps://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/yeswiki-before-4.6.7-unrestricted-file-upload-via-bazar-csv-import\n","aliases":"CVE-2026-104471\nGHSA-g4m2-8g7g-xw8c\n","assigner":"VulnCheck","epss":0.37,"enisaIdProduct":[{"id":"b8589dde-6bb8-3c6b-a330-e67428958f43","product":{"name":"yeswiki","vendor":{"name":"YesWiki"}},"product_version":"0 \u003c4.6.7"}],"enisaIdVendor":[{"id":"90a7023e-177c-3168-9f69-5d84c6594ec7","vendor":{"name":"YesWiki"}}]},{"id":"EUVD-2026-91579","enisaUuid":"ecc51a16-d29c-3d39-b7d1-9f0376ca56d0","description":"A vulnerability was detected in Tenda AC9 15.03.02.13. Affected is an unknown function of the file /goform/fast_setting_internet_set of the component POST Request Handler. Performing a manipulation of the argument netWanType results in stack-based buffer overflow. The attack is possible to be carried out remotely. The exploit is now public and may be used.","datePublished":"Oct 2, 2026, 12:15:15 PM","dateUpdated":"Oct 2, 2026, 1:30:49 PM","baseScore":9.4,"baseScoreVersion":"4.0","baseScoreVector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:H/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:H/SI:H/SA:H/E:P","references":"https://vuldb.com/vuln/412918\nhttps://vuldb.com/vuln/412918/cti\nhttps://vuldb.com/cve/CVE-2026-104611\nhttps://vuldb.com/submit/962720\nhttps://github.com/ZaneBoden/CVEs/blob/main/Tenda-AC9-fast_setting_internet_set.md\nhttps://www.tenda.com.cn/\n","aliases":"GHSA-5xvg-86hf-5h5q\nCVE-2026-104611\n","assigner":"VulDB","epss":0.49,"enisaIdProduct":[{"id":"66a90091-42c4-360d-8ade-65062a331326","product":{"name":"AC9","vendor":{"name":"Tenda"}},"product_version":"15.03.02.13"}],"enisaIdVendor":[{"id":"37565acb-b60a-35fc-856f-5ed4b93a3e3d","vendor":{"name":"Tenda"}}]},{"id":"EUVD-2026-91468","enisaUuid":"246c8a77-dc94-3c0d-b644-b90b3014ed90","description":"YesWiki before 4.6.7 contains an SQL injection vulnerability in the Bazar filtertags action, which wraps unescaped filterN attribute tokens in quotes and concatenates them into a raw tags.value IN (...) clause. Unauthenticated attackers on default installs can save filtertags markup in a page with a trailing-backslash token that breaks quote parity under MySQL backslash escaping. This lets them inject a five-column UNION subquery to read arbitrary table data such as password hashes.","datePublished":"Oct 2, 2026, 11:38:27 AM","dateUpdated":"Oct 2, 2026, 11:38:27 AM","baseScore":8.8,"baseScoreVersion":"4.0","baseScoreVector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N","references":"https://github.com/YesWiki/yeswiki/security/advisories/GHSA-p87r-f4x4-8r4g\nhttps://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/yeswiki-before-4.6.7-sql-injection-via-filtertags-filtern-parameter\n","aliases":"CVE-2026-104457\nGHSA-f8w7-2q27-5p28\n","assigner":"VulnCheck","epss":0.28,"enisaIdProduct":[{"id":"35b9c4f6-72af-36f1-a143-2bad965f90d1","product":{"name":"yeswiki","vendor":{"name":"YesWiki"}},"product_version":"0 \u003c4.6.7"}],"enisaIdVendor":[{"id":"c5540f7b-fdab-3d8f-a067-022ef383e236","vendor":{"name":"YesWiki"}}]},{"id":"EUVD-2026-91456","enisaUuid":"c0270217-3f69-3358-87cf-7355357ee813","description":"YesWiki before 4.6.7 contains an authentication bypass vulnerability in the ActivityPub inbox that fails to bind the verified HTTP signature signer to the activity actor. Unauthenticated attackers with any ActivityPub keypair can send signed Delete or Update activities referencing a mirrored entry\u0027s sourceUrl to delete or overwrite other actors\u0027 federated entries.","datePublished":"Oct 2, 2026, 11:38:19 AM","dateUpdated":"Oct 2, 2026, 11:38:19 AM","baseScore":8.8,"baseScoreVersion":"4.0","baseScoreVector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:H/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N","references":"https://github.com/YesWiki/yeswiki/security/advisories/GHSA-rm6r-grfg-4v78\nhttps://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/yeswiki-before-4.6.7-authentication-bypass-via-activitypub-inbox-actor-spoofing\n","aliases":"GHSA-px48-25j6-h73c\nCVE-2026-104445\n","assigner":"VulnCheck","epss":0.4,"enisaIdProduct":[{"id":"759a094b-c3e0-371b-a199-be4989b50295","product":{"name":"yeswiki","vendor":{"name":"YesWiki"}},"product_version":"0 \u003c4.6.7"}],"enisaIdVendor":[{"id":"b30229f3-4fce-3d52-8bb9-8e0de359ff29","vendor":{"name":"YesWiki"}}]},{"id":"EUVD-2026-91366","enisaUuid":"d2ad63a2-d6c4-3d41-ae7a-7c3572532ca5","description":"Memory allocation with excessive size value, Improper handling of length parameter inconsistency vulnerability in Apache Thrift Dart bindings.\n\n\n\nThis issue affects Apache Thrift: before 0.25.0.\n\n\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 0.25.0, which fixes the issue.","datePublished":"Oct 2, 2026, 10:13:00 AM","dateUpdated":"Oct 2, 2026, 11:28:58 AM","baseScore":8.7,"baseScoreVersion":"4.0","baseScoreVector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N","references":"https://lists.apache.org/thread/33otcgbqd27wf6qq810q56znzbomnhg1\nhttps://lists.apache.org/thread/cxkbblyht7988p2o6yvnmd6536qmt88k\n","aliases":"GHSA-cqj7-79w2-9qmf\nCVE-2026-94633\n","assigner":"apache","epss":0.43,"enisaIdProduct":[{"id":"55bbf423-8c54-331b-a904-d3f694876802","product":{"name":"Apache Thrift","vendo